(deterministic, numpy default_rng(0)):
  * 10 of the 20 runs of every (task, template) cell -> 2 tasks x 5 templates x 10 = 100 runs (--per-cell 20 keeps all 200);
  * inside a cell, the 10 slots are split over the code labels by the largest-remainder rule (ties go to the rarer
    label), so every template keeps its banned/substitute mix (t1 W4: 7 BFS + 3 DFS out of 15 + 5);
  * one t1 run without a stored k_pre state is always kept, so the "no state" path of the readout code runs;
  * inside a cell the runs are interleaved by label, so any prefix of a cell is itself roughly stratified
    (the notebook's RUNS_PER_TEMPLATE setting takes such prefixes).
